{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey","id":1505322,"title":"Playing as the prey.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-14T10:12:50-07:00","id":1505322,"title":"Playing as the prey.","content":"It's a bit of a different idea, or not, but I thought I'd ask, have you ever played or thought of playing in a chronicle where you're not the vampires, but you're hunted by them and the goal is to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T12:02:15-07:00","id":1505351,"title":"","content":"I have played around with this concept a few times. The main issue is that mortals are too delicate to survive most game setups. Running a mortal game, especially ones which are not premade to be hunters, is like running a person who doesn't play video games through a Souls game and deleting their save file if they die.<br /> <br /> The best survival rate I had with mortals was a Giovanni game where the PCs were tagging along with a small Giovanni coterie in the hopes of being useful enough to earn the proxy kiss (ghouled). This had the benefit of everyone knowing about the vampire world, most of its rules, a chunk of its history, and most importantly many of a vampire's limitations. Some bored Sabbat rolled through the area and went head-to-head with the Giovanni. The Giovanni died and their wraiths tore apart all but one of the Sabbat before fading back into the underworld. So now the PCs have to make it out of the countryside to a city and call for support while the last Sabbat hunts them.<br /> <br /> The Players were all people who have real world experience with survivalism, some form of combat training, computers, and other useful skills. I set the majority of the game in the countryside specifically to negate their computer/technology expertise. So the PCs were making smart decisions, being tactical, and doing everything they could to keep distance from the hunter. Even so they barely survived the first night and were badly wounded. The key thing is staying alive until dawn, at which point you haul tail as fast as you can and try to cover your tracks, maybe rest for a few hours during the middle of the day, and then get back to putting distance between you and the vampire. Even with all that half the mortals died and the other half.... looked and acted like the final girls from The Descent or the original Texas Chainsaw Massacre. Covered in blood and close to losing their minds.<br /> \u200b<br /> Now for the important bit of information, what was the vampire that was chasing them? A country Gangrel with character generation base stats and only two dots in Animalism and three dots in Protean. The earth meld negated the issue of having to go out of their way to find a sleeping spot and the animalism allowed them to track the mortals and indirectly attack them constantly. If it had been a City Gangrel, no one would have survived the first night just due to Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T16:38:01-07:00","id":1505387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey?p=1505351#post1505351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have played around with this concept a few times. The main issue is that mortals are too delicate to survive most game setups. Running a mortal game, especially ones which are not premade to be hunters, is like running a person who doesn't play video games through a Souls game and deleting their save file if they die.<br /> <br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried it in Ancient Rome (Before <i>Requiem for Rome</i> was cool); mortal-players are far to fragile and any wound, knocks them out of the game. But I played a modern vampire-game as a mortal with two psychic-powers; it was awesome and I liked it more than playing a vampire; so, players would need some sort of numina. I always wanted to run a <i>Hunters Hunted</i> game. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T05:03:52-07:00","id":1505425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey#post1505322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit of a different idea, or not, but I thought I'd ask, have you ever played or thought of playing in a chronicle where you're not the vampires, but you're hunted by them and the goal is to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some V:tM books playing as mortals is mentioned and discussed, and some possibilities and options are given. (Including becoming a Ghoul or a Vampire later on during a particular Chronicle, of course.) I have very often found this option to be intriguing and interesting, especially considering the contrats and differences from usually V:tM sessions are done and played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T08:00:38-07:00","id":1505434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey?p=1505387#post1505387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried it in Ancient Rome (Before <i>Requiem for Rome</i> was cool); mortal-players are far to fragile and any wound, knocks them out of the game. But I played a modern vampire-game as a mortal with two psychic-powers; it was awesome and I liked it more than playing a vampire; so, players would need some sort of numina. I always wanted to run a <i>Hunters Hunted</i> game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing mortals in a Hunters Hunted game works for a few reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. They already know the rules and what is going on. The learning curve is really only a thing when it comes to esoteric subjects, like trying to deal with Thaumaturgical warding, ghostly minions, or ghouled supernaturals with completely different power sets.<br /> <br /> 2. The equipment is already present. The hunters will have the right weapons to kill a kindred, they will probably have a kitted-out vehicle, and either one hell of a bunker or several ways to leave town already setup, probably both now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> 3. The Kindred have no idea that they are being hunted. Unless a hunter does something stupid, the target kindred won't know about them until either an ambush or when the door to their haven gets kicked open at 10 AM.<br /> <br /> To play as Prey in the true sense, you have to have lost the element of surprise, and most likely won't have access to equipment. So really the only thing you have to work with is your knowledge of vampires, which if that is lacking means you will probably do something like try to stare down a vampire with dominate or something else equally inadvisable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T14:22:09-07:00","id":1505501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey?p=1505434#post1505434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing mortals in a Hunters Hunted game works for a few reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. They already know the rules and what is going on. The learning curve is really only a thing when it comes to esoteric subjects, like trying to deal with Thaumaturgical warding, ghostly minions, or ghouled supernaturals with completely different power sets.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is it not that a person - and a group or an organization - has to learn (and teach others, as well) and gather knowledge and information constantly and on an ongoing basis to keep up and stay current?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T14:30:44-07:00","id":1505504,"title":"","content":"Not in this game, But I played a hunter in the Hunter Vigil line who was a former ghoul cop that worked alongside other hunters when the kindred got to blatant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T11:16:41-07:00","id":1505570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505322-playing-as-the-prey?p=1505501#post1505501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, is it not that a person - and a group or an organization - has to learn (and teach others, as well) and gather knowledge and information constantly and on an ongoing basis to keep up and stay current?</div> </div> </div> </div>The concern is that when it comes to vampires, not having the correct information tends to be lethal rather than just a disadvantage. Thus the mortals rarely get a chance to learn from their mistakes.<br /> <br /> There was one game I ran where the PCs were mortals who managed to escape a pack of neonates. They were then approached by an elderly hunter who offered to teach them how to survive and hunt vampires. He had money, weapons, safe houses, and most importantly many books on vampire lore. He trained them, he taught them, and sent them against many vampires.<br /> <br /> The catch was that the elderly &quot;hunter&quot; was in fact a ghoul in service to the Prince. Rather than mind wiping mortals who survived attacks, they were given a chance to become hunters. If they said no, they would have their memories rewritten. If they said yes, the Prince would send them against any vampire that broke the masquerade or caused trouble. The &quot;safe houses&quot; were wired with surveillance to keep tabs on them and wired with explosives in case they misbehaved. The situation created hunters that were more along the lines of the Grimm tv series where they killed the &quot;bad ones&quot; rather than killing everything supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}